1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,767
Workflows let a Report Builder report work without anyone opening it:

2
00:00:05,767 --> 00:00:11,042
start something when a report is published, run or exported, and run, export,

3
00:00:11,042 --> 00:00:13,585
email or share a report as a step.

4
00:00:13,585 --> 00:00:18,860
This video shows the report events and tasks, and runs one workflow for real.

5
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:28,069
Some reports are read every morning, some are handed to people who never

6
00:00:28,069 --> 00:00:31,910
open the site, and some matter only when something changes.

7
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:38,079
A workflow starts from an event, such as a report being published, run

8
00:00:38,079 --> 00:00:40,574
or exported, or from a timer.

9
00:00:40,574 --> 00:00:44,710
Then its tasks run, export, email or share a report.

10
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:49,179
Reports under Reports can be emailed with a subscription.

11
00:00:49,179 --> 00:00:55,200
Report Builder reports use workflows instead, and the Email Report task is how they are emailed.

12
00:00:59,438 --> 00:01:01,307
Open Design, Workflows.

13
00:01:01,307 --> 00:01:05,688
This one, Share a link when a report is published, has a start

14
00:01:05,688 --> 00:01:08,588
event and a task, joined by an outcome.

15
00:01:08,588 --> 00:01:11,488
Add Event lists the events by category.

16
00:01:11,967 --> 00:01:15,022
The Reports category holds three events:

17
00:01:15,022 --> 00:01:20,865
Report Run, when someone runs a report; Report Exported, when someone exports one;

18
00:01:20,865 --> 00:01:24,517
and Report Published, when someone publishes one.

19
00:01:24,978 --> 00:01:28,030
Edit the event to limit it to some reports.

20
00:01:28,030 --> 00:01:32,078
Leave Reports empty to start the workflow for every report.

21
00:01:36,307 --> 00:01:40,659
Add Task, in the Reports category, lists four tasks:

22
00:01:40,659 --> 00:01:46,287
Run Report, Export Report, Email Report and Create Report Share Link.

23
00:01:46,746 --> 00:01:49,843
Every report task starts with the same fields:

24
00:01:49,843 --> 00:01:53,714
the Report to use, or an expression that gives its ID, so a

25
00:01:53,714 --> 00:01:58,121
task after a report event can use the report that triggered it, plus

26
00:01:58,121 --> 00:02:00,086
Filters and an Output name.

27
00:02:00,564 --> 00:02:05,437
Create Report Share Link asks for the Recipients, a Note, how many days

28
00:02:05,437 --> 00:02:11,384
it Expires after, the Most uses, whether to Allow export, and whether to email the link.

29
00:02:15,559 --> 00:02:17,243
Now publish a report.

30
00:02:17,243 --> 00:02:20,859
In the builder, click Publish on the Call dashboard.

31
00:02:21,311 --> 00:02:24,549
The Report Published event starts the workflow.

32
00:02:24,549 --> 00:02:26,931
Its Instances list shows the run.

33
00:02:28,436 --> 00:02:32,912
And Shared Links lists the link the workflow created, for the recipient it

34
00:02:32,912 --> 00:02:34,423
named, with its uses.

35
00:02:34,423 --> 00:02:36,886
The recipient opens it once signed in.

36
00:02:41,134 --> 00:02:45,716
A second workflow starts on Report Run and uses Export Report.

37
00:02:45,716 --> 00:02:50,904
Its Format is Excel, and its Media folder names where to save the file.

38
00:02:51,365 --> 00:02:54,490
Run the Call dashboard, and open the media library.

39
00:02:54,490 --> 00:02:58,546
The workbook is there, in the folder the task named, with the report

40
00:02:58,546 --> 00:03:00,245
and the date in its name.

41
00:03:04,522 --> 00:03:09,220
A third workflow starts on a timer and uses Email Report.

42
00:03:09,220 --> 00:03:15,261
Choose the report, the recipients, an optional message, and the attachment:

43
00:03:15,261 --> 00:03:17,722
CSV, Excel or PDF, or none.

44
00:03:18,198 --> 00:03:22,799
This site has no mail server, so this workflow is shown and not run.

45
00:03:22,799 --> 00:03:27,524
Where email cannot be sent, the task takes its Failed outcome, and the

46
00:03:27,524 --> 00:03:30,198
reason is written to the site's logs.

47
00:03:34,398 --> 00:03:35,940
A morning report:

48
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:40,568
a timer, then Email Report with the dashboard as an Excel file.

49
00:03:41,318 --> 00:03:42,254
A handover:

50
00:03:42,254 --> 00:03:46,718
when a report is published, create a share link for the people who need it.

51
00:03:47,468 --> 00:03:48,585
An archive:

52
00:03:48,585 --> 00:03:52,728
when a report is run, export a copy to the media library.

53
00:03:54,728 --> 00:04:00,282
Events start them, tasks do the work, and the report runs with its owner's access.

54
00:04:00,282 --> 00:04:04,006
Send reports only to people who should see that data.

55
00:04:04,006 --> 00:04:05,648
Thanks for watching.

